    [
     1,
     "Hi,<br><br>is the multiple group feature already imlemented for binary endogenous variables? I could not find it in the documentation, and following minimal example does not work:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lavaan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>n </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">300</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>z1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sample</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> replace</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># binary outcome as integer</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>z2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> factor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">z1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ordered</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">        </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># binary outcome as factor</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>g </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> factor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sample</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> replace</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> labels</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;A&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;B&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># grouping variable</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>df </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> z1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> z2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Works with numeric DV ...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>s1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;z1 ~ x+y&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;g&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># ... but not with a categorical DV:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>s2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;z2 ~ x+y&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ordered</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;z2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;g&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br>Thanks,<br>Felix<br>"
