   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "On 11/14/2012 04:06 PM, Felix Sch�nbrodt wrote:\r<br>&gt; Hi,\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; is the multiple group feature already imlemented for binary endogenous\r<br>&gt; variables? I could not find it in the documentation, and following\r<br>&gt; minimal example does not work:\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "The multiple group feature for categorical variables is fully \r<br>implemented. However:\r<br>\r<br>&gt; library(lavaan)\r<br>&gt; n &lt;-300\r<br>&gt; x &lt;-rnorm(n)\r<br>&gt; y &lt;-rnorm(n)\r<br>&gt; z1 &lt;-sample(0:1,n,replace=TRUE)# binary outcome as integer\r<br>&gt; z2 &lt;-factor(z1,ordered=TRUE)# binary outcome as factor\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "&gt; g &lt;-factor(sample(0:1,n,replace=TRUE),labels=c(&quot;A&quot;,&quot;B&quot;))# grouping variable\r<br>&gt; df &lt;-data.frame(x,y,z1,z2,g)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "&gt; # ... but not with a categorical DV:\r<br>&gt; s2 &lt;-sem(&quot;z2 ~ x+y&quot;,data=df,ordered=&quot;z2&quot;,group=&quot;g&quot;)\r<br>&gt; summary(s2)\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "Confirmed. This *is* a bug in 0.5-10. And has been added to the &#39;bugs&#39; \r<br>list on the website. However, it only affects models with a _single_ \r<br>categorical endogenous variable (eg probit regression models).\r<br>\r<br>Larger models (with more than one categorical variable) seem to run fine.\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
